  "updatedAt": "2026-08-23T10:06:15.807Z",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nVectorized, numerically stable reference implementation following exact specifications.\n\n### 💻 Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef confusion_matrix_norm(y_true: list, y_pred: list, num_classes: int | None = None, normalize: str = \"none\") -> np.ndarray:\n    yt = np.array(y_true, dtype=int)\n    yp = np.array(y_pred, dtype=int)\n    K = (max(yt.max(), yp.max()) + 1) if num_classes is None else num_classes\n    cm = np.zeros((K, K), dtype=float)\n    for t, p in zip(yt, yp):\n        if 0 <= t < K and 0 <= p < K:\n            cm[t, p] += 1\n    if normalize == \"true\":\n        row_sums = cm.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        cm = np.divide(cm, row_sums, out=np.zeros_like(cm), where=row_sums != 0)\n    elif normalize == \"pred\":\n        col_sums = cm.sum(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n        cm = np.divide(cm, col_sums, out=np.zeros_like(cm), where=col_sums != 0)\n    elif normalize == \"all\":\n        total = cm.sum()\n        if total > 0:\n            cm /= total\n    if normalize == \"none\":\n        return cm.astype(int)\n    return np.round(cm, 6)\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ for memory buffers.\n",
